	axisLabel="Price premium at auction"
	valueHeader="Premium"
	source="Source: 4,487 priced and scored Cup of Excellence lots, 7 countries, 1999 to 2026, from Alliance for Coffee Excellence results. Standard errors clustered by farm."
/>

Because entry is voluntary and only winners are published, these figures are floors on persistence, not full measurements. They still show the shape of the gap: a blind, calibrated score is priced heavily, while a farm's track record is worth a few percent, concentrated in prior top-ten finishes.

## What a usable record needs

More story will not close this gap. Producer marketing already coexists with exporting countries capturing only 7 to 16 cents of each additional specialty dollar ([World Development, via Daily Coffee News](https://dailycoffeenews.com/2025/07/15/a-closer-look-at-value-distribution-in-specialty-coffee-markets/)). A record a buyer can act on needs three things kept apart: a stable identity for the farm or washing station, blind sensory evidence attached to each lot on a known scale, and every other claim stored with who made it and whether anyone else corroborates it. That is the record Purveyors is building. As an aggregator, we see the same farm through several importers' eyes across seasons, which is the vantage point needed to turn disposable listings into a track record.

The score explains half a percent of retail price because buyers have no way to tell which numbers and claims deserve trust. Wine fixed that by making the name on the bottle mean something durable and checkable, and its prices learned to follow quality over time. Coffee's prices will start following quality when its claims can be checked and its history is kept.

---

_Catalog figures come from a read-only snapshot of the Purveyors green coffee catalog on October 2, 2026 (45 suppliers; 2,674 stocked listings). Price comparisons are correlational. Producer-identity extraction is about seven months old, so identity coverage is still filling in. Cup of Excellence figures come from public results and auction pages published by the [Alliance for Coffee Excellence](https://allianceforcoffeeexcellence.org/competition-auction-results/); farm matching across years is approximate, and results are conditional on entering and placing._
